Subject: NimBLE: ask the BLE controller for modem sleep (mode 1, main XTAL)

The prebuilt Arduino framework libraries ship with the controller's low-power
mode compiled in but switched off: the esp32s3 sdkconfig has
CONFIG_BT_CTRL_SLEEP_MODE_EFF=0 and CONFIG_BT_CTRL_SLEEP_CLOCK_EFF=0 (IDF's own
default for this controller is `BT_CTRL_MODEM_SLEEP=n`). With sleep mode 0 the
controller never calls esp_phy_disable(PHY_MODEM_BT), so the radio's PLL and
baseband stay biased for the whole time the link is up -- advertising or
connected, traffic or none. That is the reader's idle current while a static page
is on screen, and it is not something the connection interval or peripheral
latency can reduce: skipping a connection event does not turn the radio off when
the radio was never allowed to turn off.

Both fields are runtime arguments to esp_bt_controller_init(), not library
build-time constants, so this is a configuration change rather than a framework
rebuild. Mode 1 is the only supported mode and is what BT_CTRL_MODEM_SLEEP_MODE_1
selects; the main crystal is the low-power clock BT_CTRL_LPCLK_SEL_MAIN_XTAL
selects and the only accurate one available on this hardware -- there is no
32.768 kHz crystal wired, and the internal 136 kHz RC oscillator is far outside
the 500 ppm a maintained connection needs (bt.c warns about exactly that).

esp_bt_controller_enable() turns sleep on by itself once the mode is 1
(btdm_controller_enable_sleep(true)), so no further call is needed. None of the
sleep machinery this reaches is behind CONFIG_PM_ENABLE: only the esp_pm locks
and the pre-wake esp_timer are, and both exist to keep automatic DFS/light sleep
out of the controller's way, which this build has neither of.

Scoped to the two targets whose controller config carries these fields.

diff --git a/src/NimBLEDevice.cpp b/src/NimBLEDevice.cpp
--- a/src/NimBLEDevice.cpp
+++ b/src/NimBLEDevice.cpp
@@ -922,6 +922,13 @@
 #   elif defined(CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3) || defined(CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3)
         bt_cfg.ble_max_act =
             MYNEWT_VAL(BLE_MAX_CONNECTIONS) + MYNEWT_VAL(BLE_ROLE_BROADCASTER) + MYNEWT_VAL(BLE_ROLE_OBSERVER);
+        // Let the controller power the radio down between connection and
+        // advertising events. Without this the PHY is biased continuously for as
+        // long as the link is up, which dominates the reader's idle current.
+        // Main crystal: the only low-power clock on this board accurate enough
+        // for a maintained connection.
+        bt_cfg.sleep_mode = ESP_BT_SLEEP_MODE_1;
+        bt_cfg.sleep_clock = ESP_BT_SLEEP_CLOCK_MAIN_XTAL;
 #   else
         bt_cfg.nimble_max_connections = MYNEWT_VAL(BLE_MAX_CONNECTIONS);
 #   endif
